{"title":"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the given diagram, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d2eeb1d5c6fcd47ed77084f1c2e309825a405a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 80 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 100 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 120 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"452\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the fact that the sum of the angles of a right triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, the unlabeled angle in the triangle must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7ae0e020ab523e0e0ce23cb16a11af14df3077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 - 40 - x = 140 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae67dd9216d260df67680a6462d1239481b978c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> are vertical angles, they are equal to each other, giving us:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488d8ad2bf5da129532aeb0cca0e86400a3b791d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140 - x = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52c2ab63d1e906fec7c0f2f875be6740ccd2490.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 60 = 140$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d92ce069a4dae403ce5e31127d91d558dcdfee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/